# Student Learning Tools

<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; margin-bottom:20px;">

<img 
src="https://images.code.org/694418d5d24e8a432f285868df3b9644-image-1779214201653.25.40 AM.png" 
alt="Sketch Lab icon" 
style="width:60px; height:60px; border-radius:12px;">

<h2 style="margin:0;">
Sketch Lab
</h2>

</div>

Sketch Lab is a digital design workspace similar to Canva or Figma where students can annotate, draw, organize ideas, and create visual projects. In Thinking Critically About AI, students use Sketch Lab throughout the unit to apply what they learn in each lesson and continuously build their Generate and Judge Guide.

Rather than creating the entire project at the end of the unit, students revisit their guide repeatedly as they test AI systems, collect evidence, generate images, revise ideas, and add recommendations for responsible AI use.

<div style="text-align: center; margin: 20px auto;">
  <img 
    src="https://images.code.org/d70c82fc592a0a17fec6a6d02f4dc8e9-image-1779214153330.08.06 AM.png" 
    alt="A Sketch Lab canvas that includes the Generate and Judge planning guide" 
    style="border-radius: 0px; height: 300px;">
</div>

Sketch Lab helps students move beyond simply discussing AI systems toward creating a polished, evidence-based product that reflects their own thinking, experiences, and judgments.


**Up Next**: You will preview the Generate and Judge Guide canvas in Sketch Lab. This is the same canvas that students will work on and return to, starting in Lesson 3.
MARKDOWN
